shape theory.chemistry : theory.physics.particles, theory.physics.chirality, theory.physics.hadrons {
  type: definition
  layer: 0
  """
// Chemistry from Persistence Structure.
//
// An atom is an emergent shape: a nucleus (baryons, SU(3)-anchored)
// coupled with electrons (U(1) x SU(2), free in space). The coupling
// is electromagnetic: U(1) phase reference between the nucleus's
// net positive charge and each electron's negative charge.
//
// The nucleus provides the anchor (SU(3) lattice attachment).
// Electrons provide the character (standing wave configurations
// around the anchor). Chemistry IS the character space of
// electron configurations around nuclei.
//
// The periodic table is the canopy of atomic structure: every
// coherent electron configuration that persists around every
// coherent nucleus count. The structure (quantum numbers, shell
// filling rules, exclusion) generates the table. The 118 elements
// are the traces through this structure.
//
// Derives from: theory.physics.particles (electron + baryon spectrum),
//               theory.physics.chirality (mass, charge, spin),
//               theory.physics.hadrons (nuclear structure)
  """
}
